  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#concept-spellcheck-default-true\n\n> true-by-default\n>     The element will be checked for spelling and grammar if its contents are editable. \n> false-by-default\n>     The element will never be checked for spelling and grammar. \n\nThese are misleading. True-by-default does not mean always checked for spelling and grammar; the `spellcheck=\"false\"` attribute can override it. Similarly false-by-default does not mean \"never\"; the `spellcheck=\"true\"` attribute can override it.\n\nWe should revise these descriptions, e.g.:\n\n> true-by-default\n>     The element will be checked for spelling and grammar if its contents are editable and spellchecking is not explicitly disabled through the `spellcheck` attribute. \n> false-by-default\n>     The element will not be checked for spelling and grammar unless spellchecking is explicitly enabled through the `spellcheck` attribute. \n",
